// Expected: a0 at one session and a1 at two.
//
// duplicate_acceptance_no_forward.vp with one guarded message added below
// the query, to a principal that does nothing with it. The added leg is
// downstream of the acceptance being asked about and the attacker cannot
// choose what travels on it, so it can bear on nothing the query asks: the
// verdict has to be the one the model without it reports.
//
// The engine used to lose it. The duplicate-acceptance check seeded an
// install at every wire recipient of an attacker-tainted slot, and a slot's
// wire list records each recipient guard or no guard, so the guarded hop put
// Carol in m's. That seed asks the replay to install m at a leg the attacker
// cannot touch, where the value arrives by forwarding from Bob instead;
// Carol re-executes it with the signature left honest, Bob's check fails in
// her view, and relays_are_forwarded refuses the whole replay. With no
// replay the duplicate check returned false, the matching-run gate fired
// below it, and a real attack printed as a hold with no envelope
// qualifying it.
//
// A recipient reached only through guarded deliveries takes the value by
// forwarding, so it is not seeded.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	knows private sk
	pk = PUBKEY(sk)
	generates m
	s = SIGN(sk, m)
]

Alice -> Bob: [pk], m, s

principal Bob[
	_ = SIGNVERIF(pk, m, s)?
]

Bob -> Carol: [m]

principal Carol[]

queries[
	authentication? Alice -> Bob: m
]
